2026-09-23T00:56:18.7992230Z       "body": "The coverage badge in the README currently shows `coverage ??%`. The badge worker reports:\n\n```\nNo status found which matched regex ^coverage, status descriptions: []\n```\n\nNo `smokeshow / coverage` status has been posted on `master` since #14992 (2026-02-27). The last commits before it (e.g. 4fce9ce, 728b097) have `Coverage 100.00%`; every code commit after it has none.\n\n## Root cause\n\n#14992 replaced coverage's `dynamic_context = \"test_function\"` with pytest-cov's `--cov-context=test`. pytest-cov records one context per parametrized case **and** per phase (`|setup`, `|run`, `|teardown`), e.g.:\n\n```\nLinux-py3.13-no-deprecation|tests/test_request_params/test_cookie/test_optional_str.py::test_optional_alias_by_alias[/optional-alias]|run\n```\n\nThe combined data now has ~20k contexts, and with `show_contexts = true` the generated `htmlcov` grew to **~68 MB**, over Smokeshow's 50 MB site limit. Every upload fails with:\n\n```\nERROR! ... status=429 response=429: You've exceeded the site size limit of 52428800.\n```\n\nSince the status is only posted after a successful upload, it's never set.\n\nThis went unnoticed because the retry loop in `smokeshow.yml` ends with `sleep 1` when all 5 attempts fail, so the step exits 0 and the Smokeshow workflow is green.\n\n## Changes\n\n* `test.yml`: generate the HTML report with `--omit \"tests/*\"`. This keeps the per-test contexts for `fastapi/` and `docs_src/` (the useful part, \"which test covers this line\"), while dropping the per-file pages for the test files themselves. `coverage report --fail-under=100` is unchanged and still checks tests.\n* `smokeshow.yml`: exit with an error if all upload attempts fail, so this kind of breakage is visible.\n\n## Verification\n\nUsing the coverage artifacts from the latest `master` Test run (50113da):\n\n| | HTML size | total |\n|---|---|---|\n| current | 68 MB | 100% |\n| with `--omit \"tests/*\"` | 35 MB | 100% |\n\n(For reference, disabling `show_contexts` entirely gives 41 MB; this approach keeps contexts and leaves more headroom.)\n\nAlso checked the upload loop with a stubbed command: exits `1` when every attempt fails, `0` on success.\n",
2026-09-23T00:56:18.8001922Z       "changed_files": 2,
2026-09-23T00:56:18.8002432Z       "closed_at": null,
